 308 hospitalizations and no deaths. This year's tally so farâ€”just in Julyâ€”greatly exceeds the normal number of cases the US sees in a whole year. In recent years, the US has reported between 2,000 and 5,000 cases in a year, according to CDC data . With a new outbreak announced, the tally of cases is likely to continue climbing. Nevertheless, when asked about the national surge in cases earlier this week, anti-vaccine Health Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. said the situation was " under control ." Read full article Commentsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;CvIigddAX_0adDNWVK_r6Y-L9WZRA3PSCERuf3hnYTkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;FJ07n78RhH_CQSwcpVcDfhcPKFJw-cQeNS5O9CRHHY4ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;sf9zUeam0P7rLxGbCLmMxhp_P_HqKW2jLz8w6cOz7QEƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-QEm_B28ePYhntPnG3am_INaw4yd2IqDx9T6FdwDJgAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;RYcNsHgGg_HU8LepYvd87RXebI6c0MpEUR9u4oDz9_sƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;yQOg9RFVZwbL710SgrkT7IzkYzoO5Krsu51GCESejdYƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;3RZbQxQAAQcN_sfc_gXN5y6AyDcQfJ5xCOo3kRogv0Uƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkdTextƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;0j7flnxWoa-W4op_QJsl2pNAKkqg8a-AF5Tqnsxp_ZIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkqSyndicationSourceƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni://